00:34:44,719 --> 00:34:50,959
So I did. And don't be silly. You had better go to bed. Your wits are sleepy.

433
00:34:50,959 --> 00:34:55,520
The hobbit felt quite crushed. And as there seemed nothing else to do, he did

434
00:34:55,520 --> 00:35:00,879
go to bed. And while the dwarves were still singing songs, he dropped asleep,

435
00:35:00,879 --> 00:35:05,279
still puzzling his little head about Bejorn, till he dreamed a dream of

436
00:35:05,279 --> 00:35:10,079
hundreds of black bears dancing slow, heavy dances round and round in the

437
00:35:10,079 --> 00:35:14,478
moonlight in the courtyard. Then he woke up when everyone else was asleep, and he

438
00:35:14,478 --> 00:35:19,840
heard the same scraping, scuffling, snuffling, and growling as before.

439
00:35:19,840 --> 00:35:24,559
Next morning they were all wakened by Bjorn himself. "So here you all are

440
00:35:24,559 --> 00:35:29,920
still," he said. He picked up the hobbit and laughed. Not eaten up by wards or

441
00:35:29,920 --> 00:35:35,199
goblins or wicked bears yet, I see. And he poked Mr. Baggin's waste coat most

442
00:35:35,199 --> 00:35:39,920
disrespectfully. "Little Bunny is getting nice and fat again on bread and

443
00:35:39,920 --> 00:35:45,120
honey," he chuckled. "Come and have some more." So they all went to breakfast

444
00:35:45,120 --> 00:35:50,079
with him. "Bear was most charlie for a change. Indeed, he seemed to be in a

445
00:35:50,079 --> 00:35:54,639
splendidly good humor, and set them all laughing with his funny stories. nor did

446
00:35:54,639 --> 00:35:59,199
they have to wonder long where he had been or why he was so nice to them, for

447
00:35:59,199 --> 00:36:03,439
he told them himself. He had been over the river and right back up into the

448
00:36:03,439 --> 00:36:07,439
mountains, from which you can guess that he could travel quickly in bare shape at

449
00:36:07,439 --> 00:36:11,680
any rate. From the burnt wolf glade he had soon found out that part of their

450
00:36:11,680 --> 00:36:16,000
story was true, but he had found more than that. He had caught a ward in a

451
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:20,639
goblin wandering in the woods. From these he had got news. The goblin

452
00:36:20,639 --> 00:36:25,120
patrols were still hunting with wargs for the dwarves, and they were fiercely

453
00:36:25,120 --> 00:36:29,439
angry because of the death of the great goblin, and also because of the burning

454
00:36:29,439 --> 00:36:34,000
of the chief wolf's nose, and the death from the wizards fire of many of his

