00:37:22,799 --> 00:37:27,439
that I can loan. I shall think more kindly of dwarves after this. Killed the

466
00:37:27,439 --> 00:37:32,559
great goblin, killed the great goblin, he chuckled fiercely to himself. What

467
00:37:32,559 --> 00:37:34,879
did you do with the goblin and the ward?

468
00:37:34,879 --> 00:37:40,159
asked Bilbo suddenly. Come and see, said Beerren, and they followed round the

469
00:37:40,159 --> 00:37:45,040
house. A goblin's head was stuck outside the gate, and a ward skin was nailed to

470
00:37:45,040 --> 00:37:50,559
a tree just beyond. Beer was a fierce enemy, but now he was their friend, and

471
00:37:50,559 --> 00:37:54,159
Gandalf thought it wise to tell him their whole story and the reason of

472
00:37:54,159 --> 00:37:58,879
their journey so that they could get the most help he could offer. This is what

