493
00:39:31,359 --> 00:39:35,439
And in the dim shadows of that place, I don't think you will shoot anything,

494
00:39:35,439 --> 00:39:40,719
wholesome or unh wholesome, without straying from the path that you must not

495
00:39:40,719 --> 00:39:46,079
do for any reason. That is all the advice I can give you. Beyond the edge

496
00:39:46,079 --> 00:39:48,318
of the forest, I cannot help you much.

497
00:39:48,318 --> 00:39:52,879
You must depend on your luck and your courage and the food I send with you. At

498
00:39:52,879 --> 00:39:58,000
the gate of the forest, I must ask you to send back my horse and my ponies. But

499
00:39:58,000 --> 00:40:02,879
I wish you all speed, and my house is open to you, if ever you come back this

500
00:40:02,879 --> 00:40:08,398
way again. They thanked him, of course, with many bows and sweepings of their

501
00:40:08,398 --> 00:40:12,478
hoods, and with many and at your service, O master of the wide wooden

502
00:40:12,478 --> 00:40:17,760
holes. But their spirits sank at his grave words, and they all felt that the

503
00:40:17,760 --> 00:40:22,478
adventure was far more dangerous than they had thought. While all the time,

504
00:40:22,478 --> 00:40:26,959
even if they passed all the perils of the road, the dragon was waiting at the

505
00:40:26,959 --> 00:40:32,639
end. All that morning they were busy with preparations. Soon after midday

506
00:40:32,639 --> 00:40:36,799
they ate with beer for the last time, and after the meal they mounted the

507
00:40:36,799 --> 00:40:41,199
steeds he was lending them, and bidding him many farewells they rode off through

508
00:40:41,199 --> 00:40:44,559
his gate at a good pace. As soon as they

509
00:40:44,559 --> 00:40:49,279
left his high hedges at the east of his fenced lands, they turned north and then

510
00:40:49,279 --> 00:40:54,478
bore to the northwest. By his advice, they were no longer making for the main

511
00:40:54,478 --> 00:40:57,120
forest road to the south of his land.

512
00:40:57,120 --> 00:41:01,279
Had they followed the path, their path would have led them down a stream from

513
00:41:01,279 --> 00:41:05,840
the mountains that joined the great river miles south of the Karak. At that

514
00:41:05,840 --> 00:41:09,840
point there was a deep ford which they might have passed if they had still had

515
00:41:09,840 --> 00:41:14,398
their ponies, and beyond that a track led to the skirts of the wood and to the

516
00:41:14,398 --> 00:41:19,920
entrance of the old forest road. But Bejorn had warned them that that way was

517
00:41:19,920 --> 00:41:25,600
now often used by the goblins, while the forest road itself, he had heard, was

518
00:41:25,600 --> 00:41:30,478
overgrown and disused at the eastern end, and led to impassible marshes,

519
00:41:30,478 --> 00:41:35,920
where the paths had long been lost. Its eastern opening had also always been far

520
00:41:35,920 --> 00:41:40,079
to the south of the lonely mountain, and would have left them still with a long

521
00:41:40,079 --> 00:41:44,398
and difficult northward march when they got to the other side. North of the

522
00:41:44,398 --> 00:41:48,879
Kerac the edge of Murkwood drew closer to the borders of the great river. And

523
00:41:48,879 --> 00:41:53,680
though here the mountains too drew down nearer, Bejorn advised them to take this

524
00:41:53,680 --> 00:41:56,959
way. For at a place a few days ride due

525
00:41:56,959 --> 00:42:01,439
north of the Kok was the gate of a little known pathway through Murkwood

526
00:42:01,439 --> 00:42:07,040
that led almost straight towards the lonely mountain. The goblins, Bejorn had

527
00:42:07,040 --> 00:42:11,680
said, will not dare to cross the great river for a 100 miles north of the

528
00:42:11,680 --> 00:42:16,799
Carrick, nor to come near my house, it is well protected at night. But I should

529
00:42:16,799 --> 00:42:21,279
ride fast, for if they make their raid soon, they will cross the river to the

530
00:42:21,279 --> 00:42:26,079
south and scour all the edge of the forest, so as to cut you off, and ward

531
00:42:26,079 --> 00:42:31,279
run swifter than ponies. Still, you are safer going north, even though you seem

532
00:42:31,279 --> 00:42:35,199
to be going back nearer to their strongholds, for that is what they will

533
00:42:35,199 --> 00:42:39,680
least expect, and they will have a longer ride to catch you. Be off now as

534
00:42:39,680 --> 00:42:45,199
quick as you may. That is why they were now riding in silence, galloping

535
00:42:45,199 --> 00:42:49,600
wherever the ground was grassy and smooth, with the mountains dark on their

536
00:42:49,600 --> 00:42:53,920
left, and in the distance the line of the river with its trees drawing ever

537
00:42:53,920 --> 00:42:59,840
closer. The sun had only just turned west when they started, until evening it

538
00:42:59,840 --> 00:43:04,000
lay golden on the land about them. It was difficult to think of pursuing

539
00:43:04,000 --> 00:43:08,719
goblins behind, and when they had put many miles between them in Beerren's

540
00:43:08,719 --> 00:43:13,279
house, they began to talk and to sing again, and to forget the dark forest

541
00:43:13,279 --> 00:43:17,840
path that lay in front. But in the evening, when the dusk came on, and the

542
00:43:17,840 --> 00:43:22,079
peaks of the mountains glowered against the sunset, they made a cap and set a

543
00:43:22,079 --> 00:43:26,639
guard, and most of them slept uneasily with dreams, in which there came the

544
00:43:26,639 --> 00:43:30,559
howl of hunting wolves, and the cries of goblins.

545
00:43:30,559 --> 00:43:35,600
Still the next morning dawned bright and fair again. There was an autumnike mist

546
00:43:35,600 --> 00:43:40,719
white upon the ground, and the air was chill. But soon the sun rose red in the

547
00:43:40,719 --> 00:43:45,120
east, and the mists vanished. And while the shadows were still long, they were

548
00:43:45,120 --> 00:43:50,959
off again. So they rode now for two more days. And all the while they saw nothing

549
00:43:50,959 --> 00:43:56,159
save grass and flowers and birds and scattered trees, and occasionally small

550
00:43:56,159 --> 00:44:02,159
herds of red deer browsing or sitting at noon in the shade. Sometimes Bilbo saw

551
00:44:02,159 --> 00:44:06,478
the horns of the height sticking up out of the long grass, and at first he

552
00:44:06,478 --> 00:44:10,879
thought they were the dead branches of trees. That third evening they were so

553
00:44:10,879 --> 00:44:15,439
eager to press on, for Bjornne had said that they should reach the forest gate

554
00:44:15,439 --> 00:44:20,478
early on the fourth day that they rode still forward after dusk and into the

555
00:44:20,478 --> 00:44:25,520
night beneath the moon. As the light faded, Bilbo thought he saw a way to the

556
00:44:25,520 --> 00:44:30,799
right or to the left the shadowy form of a great bear prowling along in the same

557
00:44:30,799 --> 00:44:37,760
direction. But if he dared to mention it to Gandalf, the wizard only said, "Hush,

558
00:44:37,760 --> 00:44:39,840
take no notice."

559
00:44:39,840 --> 00:44:44,318
Next day they started before dawn, though their night had been short. As

560
00:44:44,318 --> 00:44:48,318
soon as it was light, they could see the forest coming, as it were, to meet them,

561
00:44:48,318 --> 00:44:53,199
or waiting for them like a black and frowning wall before them. The land

562
00:44:53,199 --> 00:44:57,920
began to slope up and up, and it seemed to the hobbit that a silence began to

563
