564
00:45:00,079 --> 00:45:06,478
Birds began to sing less. There were no more deer. Not even rabbits were to be

565
00:45:06,478 --> 00:45:11,199
seen. By the afternoon they had reached the eaves of Murkwood and were resting

566
00:45:11,199 --> 00:45:16,079
almost beneath the great overhanging boughs of its outer trees. Their trunks

567
00:45:16,079 --> 00:45:20,799
were huge and gnarled. Their branches twisted. Their leaves were dark and

568
00:45:20,799 --> 00:45:27,279
long. Ivy grew on them and trailed along the ground. "Well, here is Mirkwood,"

569
00:45:27,279 --> 00:45:32,398
said Gandalf. the greatest of the forests of the northern world. I hope

570
00:45:32,398 --> 00:45:36,799
you like the look of it. Now you must send back these excellent ponies you

571
00:45:36,799 --> 00:45:41,840
have borrowed. The dwarves were inclined to grumble at this, but the wizard told

572
00:45:41,840 --> 00:45:47,040
them they were fools. Beorn is not as far off as you seem to think, and you

573
00:45:47,040 --> 00:45:52,799
had better keep your promises anyway, for he is a bad enemy. Mr. Baggins eyes

574
00:45:52,799 --> 00:45:57,520
are sharper than yours. If you have not seen each night after dark, a great bear

575
00:45:57,520 --> 00:46:02,639
going along with us, or sitting far off in the moon watching our camps, not only

576
00:46:02,639 --> 00:46:07,680
to guard you and guide you, but to keep an eye on the ponies, too. Beern may be

577
00:46:07,680 --> 00:46:12,719
your friend, but he loves his animals as his children. You do not guess what

578
00:46:12,719 --> 00:46:17,279
kindness he has shown you in letting dwarves ride them so far and so fast,

579
00:46:17,279 --> 00:46:21,920
nor what would happen to you if he tried to take them into the forest.

580
00:46:21,920 --> 00:46:24,478
What about the horse then? said Thoren.

581
00:46:24,478 --> 00:46:31,040
You don't mention sending that back. I don't because I am not sending it. What

582
00:46:31,040 --> 00:46:35,920
about your promise then? I will look after that. I am not sending the horse

583
00:46:35,920 --> 00:46:41,040
back. I am riding it. Then they knew that Gandalf was going to leave them at

584
00:46:41,040 --> 00:46:45,359
the very edge of Murkwood, and they were in despair.

585
00:46:45,359 --> 00:46:50,639
But nothing they could say would change his mind. Now we had this all out before

586
00:46:50,639 --> 00:46:53,600
when we landed on the Kok. He said it is

587
00:46:53,600 --> 00:46:59,840
no use arguing. I have, as I told you, some pressing business away south, and I

588
00:46:59,840 --> 00:47:03,920
am already late through bothering with you people. We may meet again before all

589
00:47:03,920 --> 00:47:08,799
is over, and then again, of course, we may not. That depends on your luck and

590
00:47:08,799 --> 00:47:13,680
on your courage and sense, and I am sending Mr. Baggins with you. I have

591
00:47:13,680 --> 00:47:17,600
told you before that he has more about him than you guess, and you will find

592
00:47:17,600 --> 00:47:23,920
that out before long. So, cheer up, Bilbo, and don't look so glum. Cheer up

593
00:47:23,920 --> 00:47:29,359
Thoren and company. This is your expedition after all. Think of the

594
00:47:29,359 --> 00:47:34,318
treasure at the end, and forget the forest and the dragon at any rate until

595
00:47:34,318 --> 00:47:40,158
tomorrow morning." When tomorrow morning came, he still said the same. So now

596
00:47:40,158 --> 00:47:44,000
there was nothing left to do but to fill their water skins at a clear spring they

597
00:47:44,000 --> 00:47:48,639
found close to the forest gate and unpacked the ponies. They distributed

598
00:47:48,639 --> 00:47:52,879
the packages as fairly as they could, though Bilbo thought his lot was

599
00:47:52,879 --> 00:47:58,318
weariously heavy and did not at all like the idea of trudging for miles and miles

600
00:47:58,318 --> 00:48:03,920
with all that on his back. Don't you worry, said Thorin. It will get lighter

601
00:48:03,920 --> 00:48:09,279
